<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
  body { font-family: Arial; padding: 20px; }
  a { 
    text-decoration: none; /* removes underline */
    color: blue; 
    margin: 10px;
  }
  .btn-link {
    background-color: blue;
    color: white;
    padding: 10px 20px;
    border-radius: 8px;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<h1>HTML Links - Day 8</h1>

<!-- 1. External Link -->
<h3>External Link</h3>
<a href="https://www.google.com">Go to Google</a>
<br>
<a href="https://www.google.com" target="_blank">Open Google in New Tab</a>

<!-- 2. Internal Link (to another file) -->
<h3>Internal Link</h3>
<a href="Day7_Void_Elements_Lists.html">Go to Day 7 File</a>

<!-- 3. Anchor Link (inside same page) -->
<h3>Same Page Link</h3>
<a href="#bottom">Go to Bottom</a>

<!-- 4. Button as Link (like you learnt Card + Button) -->
<h3>Button Link</h3>
<a href="https://github.com" class="btn-link">My GitHub</a>

<!-- 5. Image as Link -->
<h3>Image Link</h3>
<a href="https://picsum.photos">
  <img src="https://picsum.photos/200/100" alt="clickable image">
</a>

<p id="bottom">I am bottom — you came here via link!</p>

<p><b>Interview:</b> href = where to go, target="_blank" = new tab</p>

</body>
</html>
